Both types use `av_malloc`-family storage, released by `av_free`, with no owned pointer fields. RC4 can also live inline. RIPEMD is opaque in the public API; I’ll pair its allocator with initialization and prevent the zero-filled, not-yet-initialized context from reaching the safe API. I’ll also reject empty RC4 keys, which C reads out of bounds.
