* 256 + j) as u32));         safe.as_mut().set_p(p);         safe.as_mut().set_s(s);         // SAFETY: the inline reference context is exclusively owned; raw         // projection writes the entire valid arrays without forming references.         unsafe {             addr_of_mut!(reference.p).write(p);             addr_of_mut!(reference.s).write(s);         }         assert_eq!(safe.as_ref().p(), reference.p);         assert_eq!(safe.as_ref().s(), reference.s);         // SAFETY: the box's pointer addresses a live initialized AVBlowfish;         // no mutable handle or foreign writer is live during these reads.         unsafe {             assert_eq!(addr_of!((*safe.as_c_ptr()).p).read(), p);             assert_eq!(addr_of!((*safe.as_c_ptr()).s).read(), s);         }     } } EOF cat > crustify/rust/ffmpeg/tests/equiv/camellia.rs <<'EOF' use ffmpeg::libavutil::{camellia::{Camellia, CamelliaBox}, ffi};  #[test] fn lifecycle_sequences_match_c() {     // SAFETY: C returns a fresh zero-filled full-sized context, or NULL.     // CamelliaBox's Heap policy frees it once with av_free; no C pointer is kept.     let reference = unsafe { CamelliaBox::from_c(ffi::av_camellia_alloc()) }.unwrap();     let mut safe = Camellia::new(&[0; 16]).unwrap();     for len in [16, 24, 32, 16, 32, 24] {         let key: Vec<u8> = (0..len).map(|i| (i * 37) as u8).collect();         // SAFETY: full writable C context, exact readable key size and valid         // key bit count. This is the sole Camellia equivalence test, so raw SP         // accesses do not run concurrently with any init or crypt call.         let status = unsafe { ffi::av_camellia_init(reference.as_c_ptr(), key.as_ptr(), len * 8) };         assert_eq!(status, 0);         safe.as_mut().init(&key).unwrap();         drop(key);         for decrypt in [0, 1] {             let source = [0x57; 32];             let (mut a, mut b) = ([0; 32], [0; 32]);             let (mut iv_a, mut iv_b) = ([0x93; 16], [0x93; 16]);             for cbc in [false, true] {                 let pa = if cbc { iv_a.as_mut_ptr() } else { core::ptr::null_mut() };                 let pb = if cbc { iv_b.as_mut_ptr() } else { core::ptr::null_mut() };                 // SAFETY: initialized full-sized independent contexts; both                 // destinations and source hold two blocks; IVs are writable                 // 16-byte locals or NULL. These sequential calls retain nothing.                 unsafe {                     ffi::av_camellia_crypt(reference.as_c_ptr(), a.as_mut_ptr(), source.as_ptr(), 2, pa, decrypt);                     ffi::av_camellia_crypt(safe.as_c_ptr(), b.as_mut_ptr(), source.as_ptr(), 2, pb, decrypt);                 }                 assert_eq!(a, b);                 assert_eq!(iv_a, iv_b);             }         }         // A rejected reinitialization must not disturb the usable schedule.         assert!(safe.as_mut().init(&[0; 15]).is_err());         let (mut a, mut b) = ([0; 16], [0; 16]);         // SAFETY: initialized contexts, one readable/writable block, NULL IV;         // exclusive sequential raw access, with no retained pointers.         unsafe {             ffi::av_camellia_crypt(reference.as_c_ptr(), a.as_mut_ptr(), [0x72; 16].as_ptr(), 1, core::ptr::null_mut(), 0);             ffi::av_camellia_crypt(safe.as_c_ptr(), b.as_mut_ptr(), [0x72; 16].as_ptr(), 1, core::ptr::null_mut(), 0);         }         assert_eq!(a, b);     } } EOF python3 - <<'PY' from pathlib import Path for suite in ['ub_safe', 'equiv']:  p=Path(f'crustify/rust/ffmpeg/tests/{suite}/main.rs')  s=p.read_text().replace('mod bprint;', 'mod bprint;\nmod blowfish;\nmod camellia;')  p.write_text(s) PY cat > crustify/rust/ffmpeg/tests/ub_safe/compile_fail/blowfish_parent_drop.rs <<'EOF' use ffmpeg::libavutil::blowfish::Blowfish; fn main() {     let owner = Blowfish::new_boxed(b"key").unwrap();     let shared = owner.as_ref();     drop(owner);     let _ = shared.p(); } EOF cat > crustify/rust/ffmpeg/tests/ub_safe/compile_fail/b